info.description:
Full regression + feature test suite for the easyurl.in backend.

PREREQUISITES:
1. Server running locally (default assumes http://localhost:3000 - update the baseUrl variable if different).
2. Three subscribers must already exist in Postgres:
   - api_key = 'test-key-123', plan_id = 1 (Free), trial_end_date = CURRENT_DATE + 30 days (active trial), account_status = 'active' — general Free fixture
   - api_key = 'pro-test-key-456', plan_id = 2 (Pro), account_status = 'active'
   - api_key = 'expired-test-key-789', plan_id = 1 (Free), trial_end_date = yesterday (expired trial), account_status = 'active' — used for analytics 403 + redirect 410 tests
3. Free plan features must include: {"analytics_requires_active_trial": true, "requires_signup_after_trial": true}

SQL to reset test-key-123 to active trial:
  UPDATE subscribers SET trial_end_date = CURRENT_DATE + INTERVAL '30 days' WHERE api_key = 'test-key-123';

SQL to create or reset expired-test-key-789 (safe to re-run):
  INSERT INTO subscribers (api_key, plan_id, trial_end_date)
  VALUES ('expired-test-key-789', 1, CURRENT_DATE - INTERVAL '1 day')
  ON CONFLICT (api_key) DO UPDATE SET trial_end_date = CURRENT_DATE - INTERVAL '1 day';

HOW TO RUN: Use Collection Runner (top right 'Run' button on the collection) and run ALL folders in order with 1 iteration. Later requests depend on variables captured by earlier ones, so order matters - don't run folders individually out of sequence on a fresh DB.

NOTE ON RE-RUNNING: Each full run accumulates URLs for the Free and expired-Free subscribers. Run ALL of the following SQL in DBeaver before re-running the collection:

-- 1. Pro subscriber (pro-test-key-456) — accumulates URLs across every run; clear first to avoid hitting the plan cap
DELETE FROM clicks WHERE url_id IN (SELECT id FROM urls WHERE subscriber_id = (SELECT id FROM subscribers WHERE api_key = 'pro-test-key-456'));
DELETE FROM urls WHERE subscriber_id = (SELECT id FROM subscribers WHERE api_key = 'pro-test-key-456');

-- 2. Free subscriber (test-key-123) — Folder 7 pushes to the 5-URL cap
DELETE FROM clicks WHERE url_id IN (SELECT id FROM urls WHERE subscriber_id = (SELECT id FROM subscribers WHERE api_key = 'test-key-123'));
DELETE FROM urls WHERE subscriber_id = (SELECT id FROM subscribers WHERE api_key = 'test-key-123');

-- 3. Expired-Free subscriber (expired-test-key-789) — Folder 2 creates 1 URL per run, also hits cap after 5 runs
DELETE FROM clicks WHERE url_id IN (SELECT id FROM urls WHERE subscriber_id = (SELECT id FROM subscribers WHERE api_key = 'expired-test-key-789'));
DELETE FROM urls WHERE subscriber_id = (SELECT id FROM subscribers WHERE api_key = 'expired-test-key-789');

-- 4. Trial subscribers created by Folder 9
DELETE FROM clicks WHERE url_id IN (SELECT id FROM urls WHERE subscriber_id IN (SELECT id FROM subscribers WHERE api_key LIKE 'sk_%'));
DELETE FROM urls WHERE subscriber_id IN (SELECT id FROM subscribers WHERE api_key LIKE 'sk_%');
DELETE FROM subscribers WHERE api_key LIKE 'sk_%';

-- 5. Redis rate-limit counter (persists 24 hours — only needed if re-running within the same day)
-- redis-cli -h <host> -p 6379 -a <password> DEL trial_key_count:::1

-- 6. Folder 11 moderation state (before re-running moderation tests)
DELETE FROM malicious_urls WHERE domain = 'testsafebrowsing.appspot.com';
DELETE FROM flagged_domains WHERE domain = 'testsafebrowsing.appspot.com';
DELETE FROM urls WHERE short_code = 'blocked-test';
